# F5 on a file with a syntax error: the compiler fails, the status line says
# so, the panel opens with what it said. The first line of the output names no
# place and is the text colour; the second names line 4 and is in the error
# colour (232, 120, 128). The panel starts at y = 441 with a hairline and its
# rows are 22 high from y = 442.
# files bad.cm=class Main from IO\n  def main:\n    Int x = \n  end\nend\n
# open bad.cm
# args --catmintc @ROOT@/catmintc
# frames 4
# expect message build failed
# expect panel 1 2
# pixels 0 442 960 464 232 120 128 none
# pixels 0 464 960 486 232 120 128 some
1 key f5
